WEBVTT

00:00:10.000 --> 00:00:14.000
It appears that the rocks at Meridiani were not just altered or modified by water,

00:00:14.000 --> 00:00:19.000
they were actually formed in water, perhaps a shallow salty sea.

00:00:19.000 --> 00:00:26.000
The Opportunity rover has sent back conclusive evidence of sedimentation on the surface of Meridiani Planum.

00:00:26.000 --> 00:00:31.000
Sedimentation occurs when materials are deposited on the bottom of a body of moving water and create layered rocks.

00:00:31.000 --> 00:00:37.000
Those rocks can then help geologists figure out what type of water was on the surface,

00:00:37.000 --> 00:00:40.000
how much of it was there, and even how fast it was moving.

00:00:40.000 --> 00:00:44.000
Scientists working on the rover project believe that Meridiani may have been the shoreline of a

00:00:44.000 --> 00:00:55.000
large body of salt water that slowly formed the rocks found on this area of the martian surface.

